    "body": "fix on issue/4045-sodick-ln2w-dialect · PR #4065 · pinned by `pins::the_start_sequence_is_the_owners_and_no_unit_word_is_written`, `pins::a_taper_posts_tp_tn_and_g51_g52_a_with_g50_before_the_upright_move`, `pins::a_taper_without_its_heights_or_its_dialect_is_refused_by_name`, `pins::a_skim_pass_takes_the_low_flushing_word_and_its_own_condition`, `pins::a_control_side_wire_offset_is_refused_by_name` (`script_sodick_ln2w`), the 7 tests of `wire_post::sodick_aq600l` with the three goldens under `nc/sodick-ln2w/`, and `table_to_part_bottom_is_a_wire_length_of_zero_or_more` · merges at the next cut\n\nTwo items need a person before the PR is flagged ready:\n\n- The AQ600L figures in `sodick-aq600l.mch` (X/Y 600 x 400 mm, U/V 120 x 120 mm, taper +-20 degrees) are not checked against a published Sodick source. The session could not open a web page. The machine file and the decision file say so.\n- The corner rule `mitre` of the machine file is not confirmed for the LN2W control. The owner can tell what the control cuts at a sharp corner under `G51` / `G52`.\n\nNot done here: wire offset by `G41` / `G42` with `H` registers (the path stays the wire-centre path, as in the owner's start sequence), 4-axis cuts (#2130), and the refresh of the dry-run kit (it is in a different repository). The PR body lists each item.\n",
